        "problem": "Given $X\u223c\\text{Geom}(0.4),$ compute $P(X=2).$\n\n$P(X=2)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        "worked_solution": "If $X\u223c\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,\u2026 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X\u223c\\text{Geom}(0.4),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(0.6)^{x-1}(0.4), & x=1,2,3,\u2026 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2) & =f(2) \\\\  & =(0.6)^{1}(0.4) \\\\  & =0.24.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
